WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.588 --> 00:00:16.814
"It's right, Nora," Henry said.

2
00:00:17.874 --> 00:00:20.275
He was relieved that they'd finally solved the mystery.

3
00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:22.276
"Just tell us where it is."

4
00:00:22.296 --> 00:00:25.137
"Patches is mine!"

5
00:00:25.298 --> 00:00:26.018
Nora cried.

6
00:00:26.038 --> 00:00:28.099
"She's mine!"

7
00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:30.740
"We know," Cole said.

8
00:00:31.404 --> 00:00:34.086
"But you can't just take other people's stuff, okay?

9
00:00:34.946 --> 00:00:36.307
You need to give it back now."

10
00:00:37.448 --> 00:00:38.608
Nora stopped crying.

11
00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:40.369
Now she looked stubborn.

12
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.771
"You're not the boss of me!"

13
00:00:43.111 --> 00:00:43.631
she said.

14
00:00:44.912 --> 00:00:46.033
Maggie looked impatient.

15
00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:47.814
"Just hand it over.

16
00:00:48.654 --> 00:00:50.975
There's not much time left before the judging starts."

17
00:00:51.956 --> 00:00:52.997
Cole looked at his phone.

18
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:54.978
"Ten minutes," he said.

19
00:00:54.998 --> 00:00:58.360
"That's plenty of time to get the painting back in place."

20
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.522
Henry crouched down in front of Nora.

21
00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:06.864
"Please give it back, Nora," he said.

22
00:01:06.884 --> 00:01:09.466
"We won't yell at you, we promise."

23
00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:13.229
"Okay." Nora sniffled.

24
00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.012
Then she reached into the pocket of her shorts.

25
00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:18.013
"What are you doing?"

26
00:01:18.273 --> 00:01:19.054
Maggie demanded.

27
00:01:19.074 --> 00:01:21.216
"Show us where you hid the painting!"

28
00:01:22.257 --> 00:01:23.878
Nora pulled something out of her pocket.

29
00:01:23.898 --> 00:01:26.780
"Here," she said, shoving it at Henry.

30
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.044
"I didn't break it, even though Mommy thinks I break everything."

31
00:01:32.064 --> 00:01:33.846
Henry stared at the item in surprise.

32
00:01:34.606 --> 00:01:35.587
It was a cell phone!

33
00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:37.168
"What's this?"

34
00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:38.189
he blurted out.

35
00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:41.172
"Mommy's phone," Nora said.

36
00:01:41.192 --> 00:01:44.014
"I used it to take pictures of Patches."

37
00:01:45.295 --> 00:01:45.856
She giggled.

38
00:01:45.876 --> 00:01:49.038
"I mean, the painting of Patches.

39
00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:53.442
That way I'll have it even if it goes to live in the museum."

40
00:01:53.462 --> 00:01:55.764
"But where's the painting?"

41
00:01:55.964 --> 00:01:56.865
Maggie exclaimed.

42
00:01:56.885 --> 00:01:58.546
"We know you took it!"

43
00:01:58.566 --> 00:02:00.368
"No, I didn't."

44
00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:01.901
Nora shook her head.

45
00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.302
"I took Mommy's phone though."

46
00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:05.843
She looked worried.

47
00:02:05.863 --> 00:02:08.005
"I think she's mad.

48
00:02:08.825 --> 00:02:10.447
She keeps chasing me."

49
00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:14.589
"Wait. You mean you didn't take Nathan's painting?"

50
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:15.570
Cole asked.

51
00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:18.532
"No." Nora stared at him.

52
00:02:18.552 --> 00:02:20.533
"Why would I do that?"

53
00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.495
Henry wasn't sure what to say for a moment.

54
00:02:24.516 --> 00:02:26.237
They hadn't solved the mystery after all!

55
00:02:26.257 --> 00:02:29.740
"Nora!" a breathless voice called out.

56
00:02:30.764 --> 00:02:31.565
"There you are.

57
00:02:32.105 --> 00:02:34.787
Don't you dare run away from me again, young lady!"

58
00:02:36.249 --> 00:02:37.730
Nora squeaked with surprise.

59
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.312
"Mommy!" she exclaimed.

60
00:02:41.253 --> 00:02:43.935
Nathan's mother reached them, looking out of breath and annoyed.

61
00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:48.559
"I've been chasing her all over this park for the past hour!"

62
00:02:48.939 --> 00:02:50.400
she told The Lemonade Detectives.

63
00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:55.064
"Here. She just gave this to us," Henry said.

64
00:02:55.084 --> 00:02:59.688
"Thanks." Nora's mom took the phone and stuck it in her purse.

65
00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:03.428
Then she grabbed Nora by the arm.

66
00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.489
"Let's go have a serious talk, Nora."

67
00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.330
She dragged the little girl away.

68
00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:13.031
The Lemonade Detectives wandered toward the lemonade stand.

69
00:03:13.931 --> 00:03:17.792
"Nora was acting oddly because she took her mom's phone," Cole said.

70
00:03:17.812 --> 00:03:19.973
"She didn't steal the painting."

71
00:03:21.193 --> 00:03:21.933
Henry nodded.

72
00:03:21.953 --> 00:03:26.074
"I'm not sure she could have reached the painting to steal it anyway."

73
00:03:26.094 --> 00:03:29.895
"It would be hard for her to carry it too," Maggie added.

74
00:03:29.916 --> 00:03:31.496
"It's pretty big."

75
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.382
"You know what this means," Cole said.

76
00:03:34.402 --> 00:03:38.846
"The judging starts in ten minutes, and we're almost out of suspects."

77
00:03:40.007 --> 00:03:41.848
Henry had been thinking the same thing.

78
00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:44.110
"It definitely wasn't Mr.

79
00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.713
Collins. He was at Mrs.

80
00:03:46.753 --> 00:03:49.135
Sweet's class the whole time," he said.

81
00:03:49.155 --> 00:03:52.818
"And Hannah and Patrick are each other's alibis."

82
00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:54.559
Cole nodded.

83
00:03:54.579 --> 00:03:59.444
"Hannah doesn't have a motive and now we know it wasn't Nora, either."

84
00:04:00.524 --> 00:04:04.727
"The only one left on the list is that sunglasses woman," Henry said.

85
00:04:04.747 --> 00:04:07.369
"But we don't know how to find her."

86
00:04:07.389 --> 00:04:11.312
"She might not even be in the park anymore," Maggie added.

87
00:04:11.332 --> 00:04:15.715
"She's probably on her way to the big city to sell Nathan's painting!"

88
00:04:16.615 --> 00:04:18.196
Henry didn't seem to hear Maggie.

89
00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:21.919
He was looking at the lemonade stand, which was just ahead.

90
00:04:21.939 --> 00:04:24.921
"I think we have some customers," he said.

91
00:04:26.282 --> 00:04:27.002
Cole gulped.

92
00:04:27.723 --> 00:04:29.344
"It's the judging committee!"

93
00:04:30.356 --> 00:04:33.818
Henry, Cole, and Maggie all recognized the three art show judges.

94
00:04:34.959 --> 00:04:36.720
One was an art teacher from the high school.

95
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.621
The second was the curator of the museum.

96
00:04:40.682 --> 00:04:42.843
And the third was a well-known local painter.

97
00:04:43.884 --> 00:04:45.044
Maggie hurried forward.

98
00:04:45.064 --> 00:04:46.245
"We're here!"

99
00:04:46.605 --> 00:04:47.125
she called.

100
00:04:47.145 --> 00:04:49.046
"Would you like some lemonade?"

101
00:04:49.967 --> 00:04:53.989
The museum curator, a slender woman with short gray hair, smiled at her.

102
00:04:54.009 --> 00:04:56.811
"Yes, please," she said.

103
00:04:56.831 --> 00:04:58.912
"We're about to start judging."

104
00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:03.005
"And that makes us thirsty," the art teacher added with a chuckle.

105
00:05:03.966 --> 00:05:06.947
The Lemonade Detectives poured each judge a cup of lemonade.

106
00:05:07.987 --> 00:05:10.789
As the committee wandered off, Henry looked at his friends.

107
00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:13.089
"What should we do?"

108
00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:13.950
he wondered.

109
00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.151
"We're almost out of time."

110
00:05:17.691 --> 00:05:18.372
Cole sighed.

111
00:05:18.392 --> 00:05:23.414
"I guess we should find Nathan and tell him we couldn't—" "There she is!"

112
00:05:23.714 --> 00:05:24.894
Maggie shouted, pointing.

113
00:05:24.914 --> 00:05:27.035
"The woman with the sunglasses!"

114
00:05:27.996 --> 00:05:28.716
Maggie was right.

115
00:05:29.376 --> 00:05:31.658
The woman was rushing away from the food stands.

116
00:05:32.818 --> 00:05:34.960
She had both hands up, covering her face.

117
00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.961
"What's she doing?"

118
00:05:37.181 --> 00:05:37.882
Cole wondered.

119
00:05:38.863 --> 00:05:39.783
Maggie looked grim.

120
00:05:39.803 --> 00:05:42.825
"I bet she recognized us," she said.

121
00:05:42.845 --> 00:05:45.147
"She must know we suspect her."

122
00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:46.688
"Let's go!"

123
00:05:47.488 --> 00:05:49.790
Henry jumped out from behind the lemonade stand.

124
00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:52.432
"We can't let her get away again!"
